{{Wireless adapter |brand=Doodle Labs |model=DL435-30 |revision= |upc= |ean= |asin= |price= |est_release_date=2012 |fcc_date= |manuf_country=Singapore |is_manuf=Yes |manuf= |manuf_model=DL435-30 |manuf_rev= |availability= |if=Mini PCI |if_bus_version= |if_connector_type= |form_factor= |vendor_id= |device_id= |subvendor_id= |subdevice_id= |id_string= |fcc_id= |ic_id= |chip1_brand=Atheros |chip1_model=AR5414 |chip2_brand= |chip2_model= |chip3_brand= |chip3_model= |chip4_brand= |chip4_model= |addl_chips= |accessible_UART=No |flags=435 MHz (amateur band), high power |ant_conn=MMCX |802dot11_protocols=non-compliant, transverted |txchains= |rxchains= |sstreams= |oui= |lin_driver= |win_driver= }} {{ProductPage|http://www.doodlelabs.com/products/radio-transceivers/sub-ghz-range/420-450-mhz-dl435-30/}}
This device allows (via transverted 802.11b/g) operation within the [[wikipedia:70-centimeter_band|70 cm band]].. more specifically, from 420 to 450 MHz.
Additional specifications, per the manufacturer's site, follow.. *Receive sensitivity: ranges from -96 to -72 dBm, +- 2 dBm **Receiver LNA gain: +15 dBm *Tx power: up to 30 dBm (1 W) *Ambient operating temp. range: -20°C to +70°C ('industrial grade') *Dimensions: noted as [[Dimensions::60 mm x 60 mm x 10 mm]]
